3,"Aymara | People Group, History, Indigenous, Culture... | Britannica",https://www.britannica.com/topic/Aymara,"Aymara. Aymaran languages. Bolivia: Traditional culture.Music and Dance Music and dance are closely linked, with music central to healing practices. Instrumental music is more important to Aymara speakers, and men are the instrumentalists, while women are the singers.","Aymara, Central",Aymaran
4,"Aymara Language - Structure, Writing & Alphabet - MustGo",https://www.mustgo.com/worldlanguages/aymara/,"Bolivia Aymara map Aymara Central with 2,098,000 speakers is the official language of Bolivia (Ethnologue).Below are some common Aymaran words and phrases. Good day. Winustiyas (borrowed from Spanish), Aski urukipan (native Aymaran).","Aymara, Central",Aymaran
5,"Aymara, Central | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/ayr/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..iVYeJjsTpHoUvZJC0g_u1yAkdt0p9CMn8-Vb5VO9Vc0,"Central Aymara is an endangered indigenous language of Bolivia, Chile, and Peru. It belongs to the Aymaran language family and is part of the Aymara macrolanguage.","Aymara, Central",Aymaran
